start navigating in this immense field, and to open up the door to a wonderful field of research. The greatest scientific experience of a lifetime!\n\n\n## Table of contents (22 chapters)\n\n  1. ### Front Matter\n\nPages I-XIII\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n  2. ### Curves\n\n    1. #### Front Matter\n\nPages 1-1\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n    2. #### Affine and Projective Space\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 3-12\n\n    3. #### Curves in \\(\\mathbb{A}^{2}_{k}\\mbox{ and in }\\mathbb{P}^{2}_{k}\\)\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 13-38\n\n    4. #### Higher Geometry in the Projective Plane\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 39-62\n\n    5. #### Plane Curves and Algebra\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 63-118\n\n    6. #### Projective Varieties in \\(\\mathbb{P}^{N}_{k}\\)\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 119-139\n\n  3. ### Introduction to Grothendieck’s Theory of Schemes\n\n    1. #### Front Matter\n\nPages 141-141\n\nDownload chapter PDF\n\n  4. ### Introduction to Grothendieck's Theory of Schemes\n\n    1. #### Categories and Functors\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 143-160\n\n    2. #### Constructions and Representable Functors\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 161-164\n\n    3. #### Abelian Categories\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 165-183\n\n    4. #### The Concept of Spec(A)\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 185-194\n\n    5. #### The Category of Schemes\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 195-215\n\n    6. #### Properties of Morphisms of Schemes\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 217-238\n\n    7. #### Modules, Algebras and Bundles on a Scheme\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 239-245\n\n    8. #### More Properties of Morphisms, Scheme Theoretic Image and the “Sorite”\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 247-251\n\n    9. #### Projective Schemes and Bundles\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 253-261\n\n    10. #### Further Properties of Morphisms\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 263-274\n\n    11. #### Conormal Sheaf and Projective Bundles\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 275-284\n\n    12. #### Cohomology Theory on Schemes\n\n       * Audun Holme\n\nPages 285-305\n\n## Reviews\n\nFrom the reviews:\n\n“The book sets out on a project to convey the big ideas of algebraic geometry in the 21st century in a way that will be accessible and that will get to get to the big ideas (relatively) quickly. … The topics … give a good overview of modern algebraic geometry, and I think that a reader who is interested in getting quick statements of theorems will find a lot to like in this book.” (Darren Glass, The Mathematical Association of America, August, 2012)\n\n“The book under review offers a first introduction to algebraic geometry of a special kind … . quite a variety of topics from modern algebraic geometry is presented to the reader, often in a sketchy or survey-like manner, but always with hints for further reading. The sections of the single chapters are mostly short, and the presentation is nowhere lengthy or tedious. … the book must be seen as a charming invitation to algebraic geometry, along some sort of ‘royal road’ (of pleasure and diversity).” (Werner Kleinert, Zentralblatt MATH, Vol. 1237, 2012)\n\n## Authors and Affiliations\n\n  * ### Department of Mathematics, University of Bergen, Bergen, Norway\n\nAudun Holme\n\n## Accessibility Information\n\nAccessibility information for this book is coming soon. We're working to make it available as quickly as possible. Thank you for your patience.\n\n## Bibliographic Information\n\n  * Book Title: A Royal Road to Algebraic Geometry\n\n  * Authors: Audun Holme\n\n  * DOI: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-19225-8\n\n  * Publisher: Springer Berlin, Heidelberg\n\n  * eBook Packages: Mathematics and Statistics, Mathematics and Statistics (R0)\n\n  * Copyright Information: Springer-Verlag Berlin Heidelberg 2012\n\n  * Hardcover ISBN: 978-3-642-19224-1 Published: 06 October 2011\n\n  * Softcover ISBN: 978-3-642-42921-7 Published: 29 November 2013\n\n  * eBook ISBN: 978-3-642-19225-8 Published